=== PART 4 -- S4/S5: the discharging rule and the distance-2 verdict ===
  RULE.  u in W_anti sends 1 to each distance-2 neighbour; a distance-2 x sends
  1 to each distance-3 neighbour.  With a = d - t and (S3) charge(y) = -2:
    final(u) = |W1(u)| - 1 - t(u) <= -1        [t(u) >= |W1(u)| by R0a/R0b]
    final(y) = -2 + 1 = -1                     [S3]
    final(x) = a(x) - 3 - |P(x)| + alpha(x) = 2alpha(x) + |Q(x)| - t(x) - 3
  where alpha(x)=|N(x) cap W_anti|, P(x)=distance-3 nbrs, Q(x)=distance-2 nbrs.
